# @hsk-sync:new-note

Token `@hsk-sync:new-note` marks one logical **New note** command in three places. If behavior, beginning templates, or personal-data settings change in any implementation, update the other two to match.

## Sibling implementations

| Block | Path |
|-------|------|
| Python action | `D:\GitHub\harrix-swiss-knife\src\harrix_swiss_knife\actions\markdown\new_markdown.py` |
| Beginning snippets / config | `D:\GitHub\harrix-swiss-knife\config\beginning-of-*.md`, `personal_data` in config |
| VS Code (JS) | `D:\GitHub\harrix-swiss-knife\vscode\harrix-notes-explorer-hsk\new-note.js` |
| Android (this repo) | create note + New note settings (`NotesTreeRepository`, `NotesViewerPreferences`, `SettingsScreen`, `NotesCreateNoteDialog`) |

## Shared contract

1. Choose a beginning template (picker when interactive; default/first otherwise).
2. Body: beginning text + `\n# {heading}\n\n\n`.
3. `personal_data.enabled` default **false** — omit `author` / `author-email` when off; inject configured values when on (defaults `noname` / empty).
4. Layout: folder-per-note `{stem}/{stem}.md` (Desktop, JS, and Android).

Out of scope for this sync id: Diary/Dream/Cases, rich markdown templates, Android-only canvas notes (`type: canvas` + `img/canvas_01.png`).

Later synced commands use their own `@hsk-sync:<id>` + rule file using this pattern.
